Consider the following recursive C function that takes two arguments:
<pre><code class="c">unsigned int foo (unsigned int n, unsigned int r) {
  if (n &gt; 0) return((n % r) + foo(n/r, r));
  else return 0;
}</code></pre>
What is the return value of the function foo when it is called as <b>foo (345, 10)</b>?

